import Lean

/-! The MCP Apps view for LeanFM's session tools (clause selfhost.mcp.session.view, decision
session-view). One static HTML document, compiled in. It draws a result's diagram from LeanFM's
shapes with createElementNS, animates its event stream on a canvas drawn like the Kerberos video's trace (near-black stage, dashed slate lifelines, blue requests, green replies, red refusals, gold local events, each arrow labelled with its event id), scrolled both ways inside its panel (one row per event, lifelines spaced for the longest label, each arrow's words in two lines (event id and message above it, route and status below) so the diagram needs about half the width, following the newest event until the user scrolls) with more detail on from the start, the stream as a monospaced log beside it and the current or selected event as coloured JSON under the log; a bar above the stream lists every session LeanFM derived from the protocol's where-clause equations and the events' cause and prior links (its key and event count) and the unattributed events, and picking one plays only that session, each event keeping its id and its JSON as sent, the roles with no event left named as hidden, while the log keeps each event's simulated session number as a cross-check; calls in the generated diagram fold to one double-headed arrow (depth 2 and below start folded) and roles used only inside folded calls are hidden and named in a note that opens them again; an OpenAPI button beside Protobuf asks session_openapi for every role and shows the document of each role that serves a routed request, as YAML coloured by key, string and literal (spans and text nodes only, no HTML parsed); Properties builds a formula from a pattern and messages read from the protocol text (A can happen, always happens, never happens, after A the session can still end, after A B always follows, can still happen, never happens, B only after A); Animate generates the number of sessions set beside it (1 to 200) and tries up to eight seeds, keeping the first stream in which every role takes part and saying which seed; in the stream each cause is a bracket in a gutter (overlapping ones in lanes) and clicking an event focuses on its thread through prior links, the other events and the roles left without one disappearing until Show all events; shows every other field as
text, and edits the protocol as LeanFM protocol text, rechecking it through the host's tools/call; it
declares no network domains (editing Lean text; session_conform's problems show as issues; the animation starts in full detail; a Full screen button, shown when the host offers full screen, asks the host to show the view in its side panel or full screen and to bring it back, the animation then filling the height; A- and A+ beside it scale the whole view (text, diagrams and canvases, 50% to 150%) with CSS zoom, canvases kept sharp and pointer positions divided by the scale; arrows drawn thicker than frames; text haloed; walk-through via session_next; script checked with node --check; no choice symbols; counterexample and compatibility panels; a sketch that adds messages by clicking lifelines, trimming a split brace, offering replies only to requests; MDP terminal balances, expected net balances and the chain view's expected visits, outcomes and duration, walks' realized rewards and horizon totals as text; a navigation bar for the whole protocol, each role's view, its OpenAPI and protobuf, and a generated dataset drawn as bar charts; session_explore's tree listed like a file explorer (indented rows, open/close arrows, no canvas, pan or zoom), folded at the start, opened by click or keys, with a node's source, a protocol's diagram or a role's view beside it; a dataset whose sessions each take their own order folds its path chart; room after the longest bar for its count; a message's payload, a role's state machine and the grammar walk, all on canvas; the walk keeps its panel and the camera follows it; a newer layout stops an older tween; a step taken before keeps its known edge; a protocol picked from the list draws its own diagram at once, with a state machine per role and its own grammar walk; a sequence diagram folds: a click on a frame header folds or opens it, an included protocol starts folded and can show its roles' state machines instead, a click on an actor shows its state machine, and every drawing has a collapse button; whatever is picked in the tree is drawn, its own part highlighted and the frames around it opened, and a click on an arrow or a frame header shows the source it was drawn from; in the tree a click selects a row and only its arrow, a double click or Enter opens it; up and down move through the rows shown, right opens or steps in, left closes or steps out, Home and End; a defined protocol in the tree opens to its own steps; panels that fold say so in a header button; the diagram's clickable parts outline on hover and each actor is marked "states"; a result with no shapes falls back to its SVG; a role picked in the tree or the navigation bar opens on its state machine drawn on canvas, its typestate text and message table folded below; after an edit the tree LeanFM gives back keeps what was open and selected, and the selected node is drawn again from the new text; a state machine no longer stops the tree beside it from drawing; every view is one click away in a bar grouped as structure (whole protocol, tree, review, protobuf), roles, behaviour (animation, walk-through, decision process, dataset), properties (CTL with presets and a JSON form, requirements, instances) and code (Python and TypeScript skeletons), the view shown lit and regenerated after an edit; a message in the tree asks session_ctl whether it can happen, always happens, and whether the session can still end after it; the view is read-only: the protocol source is shown folded, with no insert buttons and no sketch; a role's view walks one generated run event by event with every actor's lifeline, its own events marked, the events listed beside the drawing and clickable; an included protocol's frame has an "open Name" link that jumps into that protocol: in the tree it selects the protocol's node, opening the nodes above it, elsewhere the drawing is replaced by the included protocol's own with a trail of buttons back; a role's state machine is drawn from the layout LeanFM computes (selfhost.session.layout): rounded boxes named by what just happened, a double border where the session may end, columns by depth, edges along LeanFM's routes, structural steps dashed and named, the whole drawing fitted to the visible width at any zoom, refitted on resize and full screen until the user zooms or pans (0 refits); A- reaches 10%; in full screen every diagram shrinks to the width, with the old circle layout only when an answer carries no layout). Above everything, a dark navigator bar (clause selfhost.mcp.session.navigator) shows the distillation chain chat → book → requirements → code and a project picker (LeanFM by default); each stage is drawn from project_view: the saved conversation log as text with no input, one PNG page of the book with previous and next, the tasks with their CTL properties and where_ guards, the clauses and the protocol files (one opens in session_explore's tree), and the source tree with traceability counts, a picked file's text and its mappings; in an event stream each thread (an actor's own order, its prev chain, as LeanFM names it) is drawn in its own colour, its arrows and log rows alike, with a legend, and a highlight that lights one session or thread in the whole stream and fades the rest; a focus frames the sessions its events formed, a child inside its parent, room left above the first row for the outermost tab; a log naming instances draws one lifeline per actor, its log rows naming the actors; a joined session is framed under its first parent, its tab naming every parent. The spec stage's requirements and implementations sections list every entry (selfhost.requirements.list), each with its kind, file, verdict or computed status and the CTL it converts to, and open it in the viewer of its kind: a protocol in the explorer, a formula in the CTL view by its file and formula, a sorry, hint or evidence as text; the badge stands apart from the summary text. Lake does not track include_str, so a change to the HTML needs a change here too. -/

namespace LeanFM.MCP
open Lean

def sessionViewUri : String := "ui://leanfm/session-view"
def sessionViewHtml : String := include_str "SessionView.html"

/-- The session view in a whole browser window (clause selfhost.mcp.session.standalone): a host page
served by make serve at /view that frames the view (served at /view/app) with scripts only, answers
its MCP Apps handshake as a full-screen host, forwards its tools/call to /mcp for the view's tools only,
and opens on project_view for the project, stage and impl in the address. -/
def sessionHostHtml : String := include_str "SessionHost.html"

def sessionHostPolicy : String :=
  "default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; frame-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'"

def sessionAppPolicy : String :=
  "default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src data:; connect-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'"

/-- The tools whose results the session view draws. -/
def sessionViewTools : List String := ["session_check", "session_diagram", "session_mdp", "session_simulate", "session_conform", "session_ctl", "session_compat", "session_actor", "session_dataset", "session_openapi", "session_types", "session_explore", "session_review", "session_sla", "session_instances", "session_skeleton", "project_view"]

/-- The tools the standalone host page forwards: the ones the view draws, and session_next. -/
def sessionHostTools : List String := sessionViewTools ++ ["session_next"]

def sessionViewToolMeta : Json :=
  Json.mkObj [("ui", Json.mkObj [("resourceUri", sessionViewUri)])]

/-- Attach the session view to a tool definition when the view draws that tool. -/
def withSessionView (tool : Json) : Json :=
  match tool.getObjValAs? String "name" with
  | .ok name => if sessionViewTools.contains name then tool.setObjVal! "_meta" sessionViewToolMeta else tool
  | .error _ => tool

end LeanFM.MCP
